        "Abstract": "This paper presents Jamp, a Japanese NLI dataset for temporal inference, and evaluates the generalization capacity of several language models on this dataset. The dataset is constructed using a template-based approach to ensure diversity and control over the vocabulary and inference patterns. The authors evaluate several pre-trained language models on the dataset in zero-shot and fine-tuning settings."
